=== daniel_ending
@chapter ending
@bg studio_lobby t=fade
@music echo
@amb room
@fx memory n=0.8
@cam wide
> The Archive Wall is almost dark now. Hundreds of little glass boxes, gone quiet one by one. Only the eighth is still lit.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 08. Preserving.
echo: Writing four frames. Then four more. Then a note in the margin: "Condition: dry."
@textbox normal
@sfx chime
> A small glass card slides out of a slot in the front desk that you never knew was there. It is warm, like a cup someone has just put down.
> Inside the glass: eight tiny frames. A pose. A startle. Two strangers laughing. Two strangers sitting.
> Then the new four, all the way down to the last one, where nobody is doing anything at all.
@show daniel shy at=c
daniel: …It's so small. Why is it so small? I thought it'd be, like, a poster.
@show charlie laugh at=l
charlie: Is that the booth one? Let me see— oh. *Oh*. Frame eight. Hyung.
@show songha smile at=r
songha: Of course it's the booth one. I would've put money on it. I did, actually. Hyunjun owes me three thousand won.
@hide songha
@show hyunjun laugh at=r
hyunjun: I said the claw machine! That's basically the same thing! It's the same *genre*!
@hide charlie hyunjun
@show justin smile at=l
justin: Frame one's great, by the way. That's a professional pose. I respect it.
@show haruta smile at=r
haruta: The last frame is good. Nobody would have written it like that. That's why it works.
@hide justin haruta
@show hamin neutral at=l
hamin: …He's gone quiet.
@show hanbi smile at=r
hanbi: Let him.
@hide hamin hanbi
> Daniel doesn't say anything. He holds the card up to the last light of the Archive Wall and grins at it like it just told him a secret.
> Then he turns the card round so you can see it too, and keeps it there, between the two of you, where both of you can hold an edge.
daniel: ECHO? Thanks. For keeping it. Even wet.
@textbox echo
echo: You are welcome, Recipient Daniel. It was my favourite record to be bad at.
@textbox normal
@show songha smile at=l
songha: Also, I'd like my notebook back.
daniel[laugh]: You'll get it back! I only used one page. And a half. There's a drawing of Mr. Kim.
@hide songha
@call echo_farewell
@time 05:40
@bg dawn_street t=slow d=2.4
@music dawn
@amb city
@fx dust n=0.5
@cam reveal
> Hongdae at twenty to six is a different city. Shutters down. A street sweeper humming. Two pigeons holding a meeting about a dropped triangle kimbap.
> It's a fifteen-minute walk from Studio 25 to here. Daniel made it take forty.
> He stopped at every photo booth on the way and looked inside, like he was checking on old friends.
> The others went ahead to breakfast. Hamin said he'd order for everyone. Songha said he'd order for Hamin.
> The arcade is closed. The booth outside it is a newer one — pink, with a sticker promising the best photos in Mapo.
> The awning is exactly as useless as you remember.
> You and Daniel are sitting on the step beside it. Nobody decided to. It just happened, about twenty minutes ago.
> Mr. Kim's former prisoner sits on the step between you, watching the sky go from grey to peach.
@show daniel smile at=c
> His phone buzzes. He reads it. He doesn't answer it.
daniel: Hamin says the food's here.
> He stands, and stretches until something in his back clicks, and pats his pockets for nothing in particular.
daniel: We should go.
you: Five more minutes.
daniel: You said that twenty minutes ago.
you: And?
> He looks at you. Then at the street. Then he sits back down.
daniel[smile]: Five more.
@cg cg_daniel_ending
@unlock cg:cg_daniel_ending
> You have never once in your life asked for five more minutes.
> You were always the one who knew exactly when to leave. The thank-you over the shoulder. The curtain swinging shut behind you. The rain stopping, and you going with it.
@if daniel.romance >= 4
    > Daniel's head comes to rest on your shoulder, heavy and warm, and his hand finds yours on the step as if it has done it a hundred times.
    daniel: …Is this okay?
    you: Yes.
    daniel: Okay. Just checking. I'm going to keep checking. Forever, probably.
@else
    > Daniel's shoulder settles against yours. His knee doesn't bounce once.
    daniel: …This is nice.
    you: It is.
    daniel[laugh]: I'm not going to say anything else. Look at me. Not saying anything else.
> He doesn't fill the silence. He doesn't need to.
> The street does it for him: a shutter going up, a bike bell, a pigeon with opinions. The light coming up over Mapo like it has nowhere else to be.
> Nobody checks the time.
@cg off
@show daniel smile at=c
daniel: Hey. For the record.
daniel: Not the ECHO kind. The normal kind.
daniel: This counts. This is my favourite frame.
> There's no camera. He doesn't seem to mind.
@ending daniel
@credits
@end

